Data designs for the app

## Tables

### User (auth.users)
- Default Supabase auth.users table
- Used as the base for user authentication

### Profile
- Extends auth.users
- Fields:
  - `id` (UUID, PRIMARY KEY): References auth.users(id)
  - `username` (TEXT, UNIQUE): User's display name
  - `full_name` (TEXT): User's full name
  - `avatar_url` (TEXT): URL to user's avatar
  - `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ): Record creation timestamp
  - `updated_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ): Last update timestamp

### Snippet
- Created audio snippets with metadata
- Fields:
  - `id` (UUID, PRIMARY KEY): Unique identifier
  - `user_id` (UUID): References profiles(id)
  - `title` (TEXT): Snippet title
  - `description` (TEXT): Optional description
  - `audio_url` (TEXT): URL to audio file in storage
  - `duration_seconds` (INTEGER): Length of audio in seconds
  - `status` (ENUM): One of: pending, processing, completed, failed
  - `spotify_track_id` (TEXT): Original track ID
  - `spotify_artist` (TEXT): Track artist
  - `spotify_album` (TEXT): Track album
  - `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ): Record creation timestamp
  - `updated_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ): Last update timestamp

### Request
- User's request for audio snippet
- Fields:
  - `id` (UUID, PRIMARY KEY): Unique identifier
  - `user_id` (UUID): References profiles(id)
  - `content` (TEXT): Natural language request text
  - `status` (ENUM): One of: pending, processing, completed, failed
  - `snippet_id` (UUID): References snippets(id) when completed
  - `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ): Record creation timestamp
  - `updated_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ): Last update timestamp

## Relationships
- Profile -> User: One-to-one (CASCADE delete)
- Snippet -> Profile: Many-to-one (CASCADE delete)
- Request -> Profile: Many-to-one (CASCADE delete)
- Request -> Snippet: Many-to-one (SET NULL on delete)

## Security
- Row Level Security (RLS) enabled on all tables
- Users can only access their own data
- Policies defined for SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE operations

## Indexes
- snippets(user_id)
- snippets(status)
- requests(user_id)
- requests(status)
- requests(snippet_id)

## Rule of thumb
- Include created_at, updated_at always
- Be conservative about relationships. Tightly make a relationship. i.e., cascade always on any instance
- Use UUID for all primary keys
- Enable RLS by default
- Add appropriate indexes for query performance 